ces wherever testing is available. Use permitted tests and analysis without building an APK. Report the actual checks performed, results, failures, limitations, and anything that remains unverified. Never claim success without evidence.\r\n12: 10. **ADB PRIVILEGE PRIORITY:** Whenever ADB use is authorized, always prefer full available SU/root privileges or relevant built-in Custom ROM functions over standard ADB capabilities, even when standard ADB can accomplish the same task. Use whichever method is best suited to the task, and combine root privileges with Custom ROM functions when both are available and beneficial. If neither root access nor relevant Custom ROM functions are available, use standard ADB capabilities. You can even force stop/kill the app, Clear Logs at system or at kernel level if you want to see the issues further, basically anything you need to purge whatever issue it is.\r\n13: 11. **CRITICAL/SYSTEM FILE & LOG BACKUP:** When modifying, replacing, or deleting any system or critical OS file (local or on-device via ADB/root), create a timestamped backup directory at `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\` and follow this exact two-stage sequence:\r\n14:    - **Pre-Modification Target File Backup (BEFORE touching live files):**\r\n15:      - *Local Files:* Copy the untouched original file(s) into `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\files\\`, preserving the full relative directory structure to prevent filename collisions.\r\n16:      - *Android/ADB Files (under Rule 11):* Create an on-device backup in the same directory (`cp -a <file> <file>.bak`) to preserve exact UID/GID ownership, permissions, and SELinux contexts (`ls -Z`), AND pull a copy with its recorded `stat`/`ls -lZ` metadata to `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\files\\`.\r\n17:      - *Verification:* Verify that the target file backups exist and have a non-zero byte size matching the originals before modifying live system files. If the backup fails, abort immediately.\r\n18:    - **Post-Implementation Log Archival (ONLY AFTER executing the `implementation_plan.md` successfully):** Do not pre-backup session logs or plans. Once the implementation is completed and verified, copy the final `implementation_plan.md` and `.system_generated\\logs\\transcript.jsonl` in full from the active session directory (`C:\\Users\\Admin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\<ACTIVE_SESSION_ID>\\`) into the same `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\` folder, along with a snippet of `.system_generated\\logs\\transcript_full.jsonl` saved as `transcript_full_snippet.jsonl` containing only the trailing entries for the completed task/turn. Verify these log files are non-zero before concluding the task.\n(no newline at end of file)"}
